      "headline": "Most delivery listings carry no allergy features",
      "writeup": "Allergy safety on delivery apps is thin: in one audit, 80% of 50 listed restaurants offered no allergy features at all[^a3c11].\n\n## Most listings carry no allergy intake\n\nSafePlate checked 50 restaurants on DoorDash and Uber Eats and found 80% had zero allergy safety features[^a3c11].\n\n**listings with no allergy features**\n\nThe allergy field users trust often never reaches the kitchen[^a3c11].\n\n| | Value | Sources |\n|---|---|---|\n| listings with no allergy features | 80% | [^a3c11] |\n| restaurants checked | 50 | [^a3c11] |\n\n## Subscriptions reach few grocery shoppers\n\nAs of October 2024, 9% of US online grocery shoppers had Instacart+, against 25% for Walmart+[^a2c15].\n\nWalmart+ reaches nearly three times as many shoppers as Instacart+[^a2c15].\n\n| | Share of US online grocery shoppers |\n|---|---|\n| Walmart+ | 25% [^a2c15] |\n| Instacart+ | 9% [^a2c15] |",
